IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa2-ch5-ch6-name-change-disclosure`

-- coa2-tests-ch5-ch6.l4: tests for coa2-ch5-ch6-name-change-disclosure.l4 (ss 77-85).
-- Every expected value is written from the text of the section named beside it, before running.
-- JUST FALSE = the text says no; JUST TRUE = the text says yes; NOTHING = the text does not decide.

-- s 77(1): a company may change its name (a) by special resolution (s 78), (b) by other means provided for by its articles (s 79)
-- (the way, "the resolution is a special resolution", the articles provide for the other means)
#ASSERT `s 77(1) the company may change its name in that way` `s 77(1)(a) by special resolution` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 77(1) the company may change its name in that way` `s 77(1)(a) by special resolution` (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- a resolution that is not a special resolution is not this way
#ASSERT `s 77(1) the company may change its name in that way` `s 77(1)(a) by special resolution` NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 77(1) the company may change its name in that way` `s 77(1)(b) by other means provided for by the company's articles` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 77(1) the company may change its name in that way` `s 77(1)(b) by other means provided for by the company's articles` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- the articles provide no other means

-- s 77(2): the name may also be changed (a) by resolution of the directors under s 64, (b) on the adjudicator's determination under s 73, (c) on the court's determination under s 74, (d) under s 1033, (e) by the directors under s 45(3) of the Charities Act 2011
#ASSERT `s 77(2) the name of the company may also be changed in that way` `s 77(2)(a) by resolution of the directors acting under section 64` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 77(2) the name of the company may also be changed in that way` `s 77(2)(b) on the determination of a new name by a company names adjudicator under section 73` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 77(2) the name of the company may also be changed in that way` `s 77(2)(c) on the determination of a new name by the court under section 74` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 77(2) the name of the company may also be changed in that way` `s 77(2)(d) under section 1033 (company's name on restoration to the register)` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 77(2) the name of the company may also be changed in that way` `s 77(2)(e) by resolution of the directors acting under section 45(3) of the Charities Act 2011` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 77(2) the name of the company may also be changed in that way` `s 77(2)(a) by resolution of the directors acting under section 64` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING -- the circumstances of s 64 are not present
#ASSERT `s 77(2) the name of the company may also be changed in that way` `s 77(2)(d) under section 1033 (company's name on restoration to the register)` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 78(1): where a change of name has been agreed by special resolution, the company must give notice to the registrar
-- (the resolution is a special resolution, a change of name has been agreed)
#ASSERT `s 78(1) the company must give notice to the registrar` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 78(1) the company must give notice to the registrar` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- agreed by a resolution that is not a special resolution
#ASSERT `s 78(1) the company must give notice to the registrar` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 78(1) the company must give notice to the registrar` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- no change agreed

-- s 78(2): where the change is conditional on an event, the notice must (a) specify that the change is conditional, (b) state whether the event has occurred
#ASSERT `s 78(2)(a) the notice must specify that the change is conditional` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 78(2)(a) the notice must specify that the change is conditional` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 78(2)(b) the notice must state whether the event has occurred` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 78(2)(b) the notice must state whether the event has occurred` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 78(3): if the notice states that the event has not occurred (a) the registrar need not act until further notice, (b) when it occurs the company must give notice, (c) the registrar may rely on the statement
#ASSERT `s 78(3)(a) the registrar is not required to act under section 80 until further notice` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 78(3)(a) the registrar is not required to act under section 80 until further notice` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 78(3)(b) the company must give notice to the registrar stating that the event has occurred` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 78(3)(b) the company must give notice to the registrar stating that the event has occurred` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the event has not occurred yet
#ASSERT `s 78(3)(b) the company must give notice to the registrar stating that the event has occurred` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the notice did not say the event had not occurred
#ASSERT `s 78(3)(c) the registrar may rely on the statement as sufficient evidence of the matters stated in it` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 78(3)(c) the registrar may rely on the statement as sufficient evidence of the matters stated in it` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 79: where a change has been made by other means provided for by the articles, (a) the company must give notice to the registrar, (b) the notice must be accompanied by a statement; (2) the registrar may rely on the statement
#ASSERT `s 79(1)(a) the company must give notice to the registrar` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 79(1)(a) the company must give notice to the registrar` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 79(1)(b) the notice must be accompanied by a statement that the change of name has been made by means provided for by the company's articles` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 79(1)(b) the notice must be accompanied by a statement that the change of name has been made by means provided for by the company's articles` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 79(2) the registrar may rely on the statement as sufficient evidence of the matters stated in it` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 79(2) the registrar may rely on the statement as sufficient evidence of the matters stated in it` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 80(1): applies where (a) the registrar receives notice and is satisfied (i) the name complies with Part 5 and (ii) the Acts and articles are complied with, or (b) the registrar determines a new name under s 76C or 76D
-- (notice received, satisfied (i), satisfied (ii), registrar determines a new name)
#ASSERT `s 80(1) this section applies` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (a)
#ASSERT `s 80(1) this section applies` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- (a)(ii) missing
#ASSERT `s 80(1) this section applies` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- (a)(i) missing
#ASSERT `s 80(1) this section applies` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- no notice received
#ASSERT `s 80(1) this section applies` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (b)
#ASSERT `s 80(1) this section applies` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (b) is enough on its own
#ASSERT `s 80(1) this section applies` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 80(2) the registrar must enter the new name on the register in place of the former name` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 80(2) the registrar must enter the new name on the register in place of the former name` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 80(2) the registrar must enter the new name on the register in place of the former name` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 80(3) the registrar must issue a certificate of incorporation altered to meet the circumstances of the case` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 80(3) the registrar must issue a certificate of incorporation altered to meet the circumstances of the case` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 81(1): a change of name has effect from the date on which the new certificate is issued (issued 10 April 2027)
#ASSERT `s 81(1) the change of name has effect on the day` (JUST (Date 10 4 2027)) (Date 10 4 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the day of issue
#ASSERT `s 81(1) the change of name has effect on the day` (JUST (Date 10 4 2027)) (Date 9 4 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the day before
#ASSERT `s 81(1) the change of name has effect on the day` (JUST (Date 10 4 2027)) (Date 11 4 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 81(1) the change of name has effect on the day` NOTHING (Date 10 4 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- no certificate issued yet

-- s 81(2): the change does not affect any rights or obligations of the company or render defective any legal proceedings by or against it
#ASSERT `s 81(2) the change of name affects the right, the obligation or the proceedings` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 81(2) the change of name affects the right, the obligation or the proceedings` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 81(3): proceedings that might have been continued or commenced by the former name may be by the new name
#ASSERT `s 81(3) the proceedings may be continued or commenced against the company by its new name` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 81(3) the proceedings may be continued or commenced against the company by its new name` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 82(4) "specified"
#ASSERT `s 82(4) the information, location, description of document or communication is specified` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 82(4) the information, location, description of document or communication is specified` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 83(1): proceedings brought by a company to which s 82 applies to enforce a right arising out of a contract made in the course of a business, in breach of the s 82 regulations at the time
#ASSERT `s 83(1) this section applies to the proceedings` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 83(1) this section applies to the proceedings` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- no breach of the regulations when the contract was made
#ASSERT `s 83(1) this section applies to the proceedings` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not a right arising out of a contract made in the course of a business
#ASSERT `s 83(1) this section applies to the proceedings` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 83(2): the proceedings shall be dismissed if the defendant shows (a) a claim he has been unable to pursue or (b) financial loss, unless the court is satisfied it is just and equitable to let them continue
-- (the section applies, (a) shown, (b) shown, just and equitable to continue)
#ASSERT `s 83(2) the proceedings shall be dismissed` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (a)
#ASSERT `s 83(2) the proceedings shall be dismissed` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (b)
#ASSERT `s 83(2) the proceedings shall be dismissed` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "unless" the court is satisfied that it is just and equitable
#ASSERT `s 83(2) the proceedings shall be dismissed` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- neither (a) nor (b) shown
#ASSERT `s 83(2) the proceedings shall be dismissed` (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- the section does not apply to the proceedings
#ASSERT `s 83(2) the proceedings shall be dismissed` NOTHING TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 83(3): the section does not affect the right of any person to enforce rights against another person in proceedings brought by that person
#ASSERT `s 83(3) the section affects the person's right to enforce his rights against another person` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 83(3) the section affects the person's right to enforce his rights against another person` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 84(3) "specified"
#ASSERT `s 84(3) the requirement is specified` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 84(3) the requirement is specified` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 85(1): no account is taken of (a) upper or lower case, (b) diacritical marks or punctuation, (c) the format or style under s 57(1)(b), provided there is no real likelihood of names differing only in those respects being taken to be different names
#ASSERT `s 85(1) no account is taken of the difference` `s 85(1)(a) whether upper or lower case characters (or a combination of the two) are used` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 85(1) no account is taken of the difference` `s 85(1)(b) whether diacritical marks or punctuation are present or absent` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 85(1) no account is taken of the difference` `s 85(1)(c) whether the name is in the same format or style as is specified under section 57(1)(b) for the purposes of registration` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 85(1) no account is taken of the difference` `s 85(1)(a) whether upper or lower case characters (or a combination of the two) are used` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the proviso fails
#ASSERT `s 85(1) no account is taken of the difference` `s 85(1)(b) whether diacritical marks or punctuation are present or absent` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 85(1) no account is taken of the difference` `s 85(1)(c) whether the name is in the same format or style as is specified under section 57(1)(b) for the purposes of registration` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 85(1) no account is taken of the difference` `s 85(1) any other difference` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- a difference the section does not name

-- s 85(2): this does not affect the operation of regulations under s 57(1)(a) permitting only specified characters, marks or punctuation
#ASSERT `s 85(2) subsection (1) affects the operation of the regulations` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 85(2) subsection (1) affects the operation of the regulations` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
